  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Economic Empowerment in the Mekong</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment is the second phase  of the  WE RISE Together women&#x2019;s economic empowerment program with UN Women. It builds on the first phase to increase the practice of gender-responsive procurement (GRP) across key sectors, shift from a narrow focus on women entrepreneurs to a more whole-of-system approach addressing the business enabling environment, and expand into Cambodia and Laos. The overarching goal is that Mekong women are empowered to equally access, participate, lead and benefit from expanded market opportunities in the subregion. It aims to achieve this through increasing adoption of GRP practices across public and private sectors, strengthen gender-responsive data on procurement, strengthen national public policies on procurement, women-owned businesses and gender-responsive enterprises, and increase market connections and opportunities for those target groups.</narrative>
  </description>
